 "_nvidia_files": "NVIDIA CUDA libraries the servers load, which neither Crow's package nor crow-nest's engine package carries: Crow redistributes no NVIDIA file. CrowSetup fetches NVIDIA's own wheel from PyPI (url, pinned by bytes and sha256) into setup/downloads, takes ONLY the members under extract, each checked against the wheel's *.dist-info/RECORD and against the bytes and sha256 pinned here, writes each to its dest and deletes the wheel. The dests are the paths the packages used to carry them at, so Boot, lib_path and the check step see the same files. A wheel is installed on its platform when a selected point runs one of its servers: the point's engine (engine.kind, default serve), and sd-server when the point has an image_server or sets CROW_IMAGE_MODEL_DIR in crow_env (Crow starts it on demand). Windows needs no CUDA runtime file: llama.cpp and sd-server link it statically there. The versions are the CUDA 13.3 toolkit the binaries are built with; the libraries are byte-identical to what the packages shipped before.",
